=== Usage ===
Each eye has {{stat|hp|300}}. After being calmed by dealing enough damage to it, it grants a certain permanent amount of {{stat|rt}} and is unlocked. Once unlocked, it takes {{stat|rt|5s}} per warp. If the player hasn't paid the time to unlock the zone and any previous zones, the time necessary to access them would be added to the travel time cost, but is reduced by {{Green|10%}}. For example traveling to {{zone|Village Plaza}} requires {{stat|rt|4m00s|icononly=1}} from {{zone|Black Lagoon}}, {{stat|rt|3m00s|icononly=1}} from {{zone|West Village}}, and {{stat|rt|8m00s|icononly=1}} from {{zone|Village Plaza}}, which is in total {{stat|rt|15m00s}} or {{stat|rt|900s|icononly=1}} but it only requires {{stat|rt|13m30s}} or {{stat|rt|810s|icononly=1}}.

Areas that the player does not need to pass through to visit any other area ({{zone|Mirrorverse}}, and {{zone|Living Cave}}) are never included.

Destinations that are not required to enter another destination are only included when traveled to. So {{zone|Barrier Street}} is only included when traveling to {{zone|Stillgore Château}}, {{zone|Colosseum (Rift)}} only when traveling to Colosseum, {{zone|The Mountaintop}} only when traveling to Mountaintop.
== Trivia ==
*By clicking and rapidly closing the interface on the Eyes, and then rapidly attacking them, anvil sounds will play and the respective Eye will yell "{{mctxt|&f|Quit it!}}" before launching the player back. This can be used to quickly reach the [[Rift Dimension#Rift Transferables|Rift Transfer Chest]] in the {{zone|Wyld Woods}} by boosting the player from the {{zone|Wizard Tower (Rift)}} with enough velocity to be able to reach the treetops with two {{Item|Aspect of the Leech}} teleports.
*All of '''Porhtal'''{{'}}s eyes are various references.
**The Intruder is a reference to the 2019 psychological thriller film [[w:The Intruder (2019 film)|of the same name]].
**The Gill-Man is a reference to the antagonist of the [[w:Gill-man|same name]] of the film ''Creature from the Black Lagoon'' and its two sequels.
**The Baba Yaga is a reference to [[w:Baba Yaga|the supernatural creature]] from Slavic folklore.
**The Bankster is a reference to the thriller novel [[w:Bankster|Bankster]].
**The Prince is likely a reference to the 2014 action thriller film [[w:The Prince (2014 film)|The Prince]].
**The 7th Sin is possibly a reference to the 1917 silent drama film [[w:The_Seventh_Sin_(1917_film)|The Seventh Sin]].
*The reverse of Porhtal is Lathrop, which is the human name of {{MobSprite|The Watcher}}.
**Porhtal could be the Rift version of {{MobSprite|The Watcher}}, but apart from the name and association with eyes, there is no proof of this.

